## Scientific And Domain Assessments

### d-limonene: omit only the source-rejected malformed CAS row

identity: supported. Targets: historical-cas-0000862.

Support RETIRE_INVALID_CAS for the complete historical cas:138-86-7 row only. The current verified owner has explicitly rejected that active identity, while preserving MIM:0000862 and its genuine legacy slug.

The raw source distinguishes d-limonene from its separate D,L entry. ChEBI:15382 defines the R form and links the d name to CAS 5989-27-5. The two-star duplicate has matching stereochemical InChI but mixed synonym baggage; I do not treat its DL labels as interchangeable. A failed check digit diagnoses the old assertion but cannot select the R replacement. The actual owner afterimage, rejected alias, unchanged original curation-history prefix and endpoint-bound source reviews corroborate that this is an applied source correction, not a pending proposal. Limits: No positive decision on newly generated mapping rows, original source bindings, roles, purity, lot or purchased form. Retain the entire old assertion and all inherited WITHHOLD history; ordinary canonical REMOVE_WITH_HISTORY remains separate.

### Furaltadone hydrochloride: retain exact-NCIT row under mandatory WITHHOLD

identity: supported. Targets: historical-cas-0001139.

Support retaining the complete NCIT:C217928 exactMatch row, including the invalid CAS:3759-92-1 annotation, as withheld diagnostic backlog.

The current owner and canonical row already identify the NCIT term as exact, so the inherited narrow-match/local-registry explanation is historical rather than a current defect. The unchanged owner still carries the malformed CAS property and the row exports it. That unresolved annotation independently warrants whole-row WITHHOLD. The hydrochloride scope, source vocabulary, original 2026-10-03 mapping date and exact-NCIT validation text remain evidence, not new certification. Limits: Do not retire the NCIT object, repair a digit, infer purchased salt preparation, or approve a role/source binding. Preserve the broader historical findings and #887/#902 scope; this review closes neither issue.

### Kanamycin sulfate: retain full sulfate row and provisional role hold

identity: supported. Targets: historical-cas-0001389.

Support retaining the complete CHEBI:6109 row and malformed CAS:25839-94-0 annotation under WITHHOLD.

The unchanged owner is explicitly sulfate-scoped, with named acid/monosulfate synonyms and provisional computational SELECTIVE_AGENT evidence. Its failed check digit is reproducible, but arithmetic does not establish that the error was a transposition or identify a replacement RN. Retaining the full row avoids falsely retiring a non-CAS ontology object or converting sulfate to free base. The historical provenance and unresolved provisional role remain intact. Limits: No repaired CAS, free-base collapse, role approval, preparation/concentration inference or whole-record/source recertification. Preserve the complete invalid token in withheld diagnostics and keep #887 open for its remaining scope.

### Methyl-2-Hydroxy-Phenylproprionate: unresolved identity stays unchanged

identity: supported. Targets: historical-cas-0001639.

Support retaining both the cas:89471-28-0 object and CAS:89471-28-0 annotation in the entire unchanged row under WITHHOLD.

This unresolved case is materially different from the two source-corrected owners: no verified new identity or corresponding completed correction exists here. The source spelling alone does not establish locants, stereochemistry, supplier or preparation. The captured later #753 comment explicitly requires unchanged/WITHHOLD, and governs over the older positive history. A checksum-derived variant would be a guess, not chemical evidence. Permanent MIM identity preserves the record without converting its uncertain mapping into support. Limits: Do not choose another CAS, ontology, placeholder or positional/stereochemical identity; do not rewrite aliases or clear the source hold. Both the earlier positive and later negative histories remain; no other #753 case is adjudicated.

### Methylglyoxal: preserve malformed annotation as held evidence

identity: supported. Targets: historical-cas-0001663.

Support retaining the complete CHEBI:17158 row, including 2-Oxopropanal and invalid CAS:79-98-8, under mandatory WITHHOLD.

The current owner is unchanged and still exports the malformed CAS property. The problem is an annotation on an ontology-target row, not authority to discard the CHEBI target. The FEBA/Hans80 source history and stored structural fields do not establish the supplied neat or solution material or any experimental role. Diagnostic retention leaves that uncertainty visible without treating the token as valid. Limits: No corrected digit or RN, supplier/lot inference, concentration assertion, stress-response role or new source binding. Preserve #887 and the complete historical row rather than scrubbing payload to make validation appear positive.

### Oxalic acid: retain full row without guessing hydration

identity: supported. Targets: historical-cas-0001956.

Support retaining the complete CHEBI:16995 row with malformed CAS:144-62-1 under mandatory WITHHOLD.

The exact predecessor/current owner and full historical row are unchanged. Invalid CAS is still present in the owner and exported annotation; no source correction was applied for this owner. The ontology label, stored neutral formula and InChI are insufficient evidence for the supplied hydration state. Whole-row retention is therefore the justified diagnostic disposition while the annotation and material questions remain unresolved. Limits: No corrected CAS, hydration inference from formula or mass, ontology-object retirement, source acceptance or full ingredient approval. Preserve the original source/validation payload and #887 hold.

### S-adenosyl Homocysteine: omit only the source-rejected malformed CAS row

identity: supported. Targets: historical-cas-0002227.

Support RETIRE_INVALID_CAS for the complete old cas:9789-92-0 row after its actual endpoint-bound source correction; MIM:0002227 and the genuine L synonym remain.

The source explicitly records Sigma A9384 and S-(5-prime-adenosyl)-L-homocysteine. The captured manufacturer sheet names that same L material and CAS 979-92-0, corroborated by the defined ChEBI:16680 L-homocysteine derivative and stereochemical structure. The S- prefix marks sulfur attachment and does not itself prove the L configuration. This is stronger than a checksum repair or generic-name inference. The corrected committed owner has removed only the disproved owner alias and retained the complete original history and negative obligations. Limits: No purchased lot, purity, hydrate, salt, solution, role, occurrence or original source-binding approval. Preserve the full invalid historical row and inherited WITHHOLD lineage; generated replacement rows and canonical retirement require their own reviews.

