## Limits And Additional Notes

- This review supports diagnostic actions, not the correctness or release of malformed identifiers. Five full rows remain mandatory WITHHOLD; all seven original scientific/source/role holds remain preserved.
- The two actual source corrections are supported here only as prerequisites for narrowly scoped diagnostic omission. Canonical REMOVE_WITH_HISTORY, new mapping rows and original source bindings need separate actual reviews.
- Primary and issue evidence was read from existing immutable captures; no fresh web, CAS database, provider or GitHub retrieval was performed or claimed. Failed captures are not treated as positive evidence.
- Furaltadone narrow-match reasoning is explicitly historical; its current invalid annotation still requires WITHHOLD. Kanamycin transposition is not inferred from arithmetic. Later Methyl negative history governs over earlier approval.
- No source/registry/lifecycle/canonical changes, native source replay, generation, full-suite rerun, merge or KG rebuild. Native review validate/save and the shared collection check are subsequent actual operations, not invented successes in this report.
- Prior S2 scientific reports were workflow references; this S3 report binds the actual new claims and endpoint and contains independently authored current reasoning. Original procedure and executing-coordinator identities remain distinct.
- No earlier finding is resolved, superseded, narrowed or closed by the empty new-findings list.

