    remain.
  details: 'The source explicitly records Sigma A9384 and S-(5-prime-adenosyl)-L-homocysteine.
    The captured manufacturer sheet names that same L material and CAS 979-92-0, corroborated
    by the defined ChEBI:16680 L-homocysteine derivative and stereochemical structure.
    The S- prefix marks sulfur attachment and does not itself prove the L configuration.
    This is stronger than a checksum repair or generic-name inference. The corrected
    committed owner has removed only the disproved owner alias and retained the complete
    original history and negative obligations. Limits: No purchased lot, purity, hydrate,
    salt, solution, role, occurrence or original source-binding approval. Preserve
    the full invalid historical row and inherited WITHHOLD lineage; generated replacement
    rows and canonical retirement require their own reviews.'
